-- title:
--   Sampled Diagonal Line Approximation Ignore First
-- statement:
--   **Sampled diagonal-line approximation after retaining the second parameter.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy with fixed field model and normalized state, let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma$ be error parameters, and assume that the strategy is $(\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma)$-good. Under the shared point-pair diagonal-line distribution, for $q=(\ell,(t_1,t_2))$ compare the left placement of the point measurement at $\ell(t_2)$ with the right placement of the diagonal-line measurement evaluated at $t_2$. Writing $\Delta=2m\gamma$, the raw operator families satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\mathcal D_{\mathrm{shared}}}
--   \left(A^{\ell(t_2)}\otimes I,\ I\otimes L^{\ell}_{[f(t_2)]};\,\Delta\right),
--   \qquad \Delta=2m\gamma.
--   $$
--
--   This is the point-pair version of the point-with-line approximation, obtained by the preceding averaging identity. It is used in the commutativity-points theorem and the ordered mixed-line lift.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.CommutativityPoints.sampledDiagonalLineApproximation_ignore_first`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
